# Environment for drizzle-kit (`db:generate`, `db:migrate`), which runs with
# this package as its working directory.
#
# Copy to `packages/database/.env`. drizzle-kit loads the `.env` in its own
# directory; nothing loads it from the repository root, and no application
# process reads this file.
#
# `db:generate` only reads the schema files and never connects, so it works with
# no value set — `drizzle.config.ts` falls back to the local development URL
# below. `db:migrate` is what needs a real connection string.
#
# Keep this pointing at the same database as `apps/dashboard/.env`'s
# DATABASE_URL: `drizzle.config.ts` and the running server resolve the value
# through the same function precisely so migrations cannot target one store
# while the dashboard opens another. The pre-split name AUTH_DATABASE_URL is
# still read when this is unset.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/code_zero_auth
